          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 8,
          "padding": 16,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "NO4X2",
              "name": "Rv t",
              "fill": "#0F172A",
              "content": "Eye-comfort verdict for Orbit field (Concept D)",
              "fontFamily": "IBM Plex Sans",
              "fontSize": 16,
              "fontWeight": "700"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "z8X1i",
              "name": "Rv b",
              "fill": "#475569",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "1) Prefer cool primary (teal/navy) for chrome — matches MaintainX/Trimble and reduces alert fatigue. 2) Put saturated green on Start/Complete CTAs (UpKeep pattern). 3) Keep amber/copper only for urgency — not the whole brand (P4 as primary fights the eye). 4) Pat2 dots stay fine; avoid busy patterns in sun. 5) Later: optional dark “sunlight” theme for outdoor sites.",
              "fontFamily": "IBM Plex Sans",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "va6kq",
              "name": "Rv pick",
              "fill": "#1D4E89",
